        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Laughton, Charles Vidor, Jon Hall\n- Works: The Tuttles of Tahiti\n- Organizations: Royal Academy of Dramatic Art\n- Roles: actor, director, producer, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Laughton was born on 1 July 1899 and died on 15 December 1962.\n- Charles Laughton was an English stage and film actor, director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- Charles Laughton was trained in London at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art.\n- Charles Laughton first appeared professionally on the stage in 1926.\n- The Tuttles of Tahiti is a 1942 film directed by Charles Vidor.\n- The Tuttles of Tahiti starred Charles Laughton and Jon Hall.",
